1
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:37,151
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,151 --> 00:02:41,151
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:41,151 --> 00:02:45,151
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:45,151 --> 00:02:50,151
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:50,151 --> 00:02:53,151
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:53,151 --> 00:02:56,151
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,151 --> 00:02:59,151
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,151 --> 00:03:02,151
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:03,151 --> 00:03:05,151
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:06,151 --> 00:03:09,151
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:09,151 --> 00:03:12,151
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:12,151 --> 00:03:16,151
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,151 --> 00:03:21,151
Separated from the rest of his crew,

14
00:03:21,151 --> 00:03:25,151
Luffy has finally arrived at Marineford to rescue his brother Ace.

15
00:03:25,151 --> 00:03:28,151
The White Beard Pirates have successfully pushed into the bay,

16
00:03:28,151 --> 00:03:32,151
but a massive number of Marines still block the path to Ace.

17
00:03:32,151 --> 00:03:34,151
The battle is heating up.

18
00:03:34,151 --> 00:03:37,151
After Luffy narrowly avoids a deadly encounter with Mihawk,

19
00:03:37,151 --> 00:03:41,151
a battalion of human weapons known as pacifistas appear.

20
00:03:43,151 --> 00:03:45,151
Look at the Bayhead! There's something out there!

21
00:03:45,151 --> 00:03:49,151
What? What the hell are they?

22
00:03:49,151 --> 00:03:54,151
Of course. I wondered when I'd get a glimpse of the government's human weapons.

23
00:03:54,151 --> 00:03:58,151
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh? I'm confused.

24
00:03:58,151 --> 00:04:04,151
The extermination strategy in action! The power of the pacifistas!

25
00:04:04,151 --> 00:04:08,151
They all look just like the Warlord!

26
00:04:08,151 --> 00:04:11,151
Kuma! No way! It's gotta be some kind of an illusion!

27
00:04:11,151 --> 00:04:12,151
Well, this just got weird.

28
00:04:12,151 --> 00:04:13,151
I think I know those guys.

29
00:04:13,151 --> 00:04:14,151
I think I know those guys.

30
00:04:14,151 --> 00:04:15,151
They all look just like the Warlord.

31
00:04:15,151 --> 00:04:16,151
They all look just like the Warlord.

32
00:04:16,151 --> 00:04:17,151
Kuma! No way! It's gotta be some kind of an illusion!

33
00:04:17,151 --> 00:04:18,151
Well, this just got weird.

34
00:04:18,151 --> 00:04:19,151
I think I know those guys. They went on a rampage here a while back.

35
00:04:19,151 --> 00:04:22,151
It's like having an army of Warlord's.

36
00:04:35,151 --> 00:04:37,151
It's not scary, I mean, fuck!

37
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:39,151
And you fuck?

38
00:04:39,151 --> 00:04:40,151
What, huh?

39
00:04:40,151 --> 00:04:43,151
I think I know those guys. They went on a rampage here a while back.

40
00:04:43,151 --> 00:04:44,151
But what do you think that it's gonna be like that?

41
00:04:44,151 --> 00:04:45,151
Please go.

42
00:04:46,151 --> 00:04:47,151
Mom, do you know that?

43
00:04:47,151 --> 00:04:49,871
But there weren't that many when they attacked us.

44
00:05:01,711 --> 00:05:04,511
Head office! Reporting in!

45
00:05:04,511 --> 00:05:06,351
You gotta hear this!

46
00:05:06,351 --> 00:05:08,831
Hello? Anyone?

47
00:05:17,151 --> 00:05:24,191
So this one's gotta be the real Kuma, right?

48
00:05:24,191 --> 00:05:26,671
I thought this was just some rumor.

49
00:05:26,671 --> 00:05:31,391
But I've heard word that Dr. Vegapunk has been working on some kind of human weapon,

50
00:05:31,391 --> 00:05:33,951
and he's been shipping out the prototypes to back up the Navy.

51
00:05:33,951 --> 00:05:34,911
This could be them.

52
00:05:34,911 --> 00:05:38,671
Well, that looks like a human weapon if I've ever seen one.

53
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:40,591
Sure, but why are they all Kuma?

54
00:05:40,591 --> 00:05:42,591
Hey, Uncle!

55
00:05:42,591 --> 00:05:45,631
This isn't looking like the plan we talked about.

56
00:05:46,271 --> 00:05:49,791
I thought the pirates were supposed to be rounded up inside the bay,

57
00:05:49,791 --> 00:05:51,951
so we could pick them off like fish in a barrel.

58
00:05:52,911 --> 00:05:54,831
Why are they scattered all over the place?

59
00:05:58,351 --> 00:06:01,631
That big guy with the axe, can you make out what he's saying?

60
00:06:05,231 --> 00:06:07,551
I believe I've deciphered the Navy's plan.

61
00:06:08,591 --> 00:06:12,591
They leaked the intel about the decision to expedite Ace's execution,

62
00:06:12,591 --> 00:06:15,311
knowing that it would send us into a frenzy to save him.

63
00:06:15,871 --> 00:06:22,431
After that, all they had to do was slowly back up their forces to fully lure us pirates into the bay,

64
00:06:22,431 --> 00:06:26,911
and then they block off the bay head with their human weapons to close the trap.

65
00:06:27,631 --> 00:06:28,351
Checkmate!

66
00:06:29,151 --> 00:06:30,431
Now it all makes sense.

67
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:34,271
That's why Whitebeard ordered us to sink those Navy ships instead of advancing.

68
00:06:34,911 --> 00:06:36,591
He saw through their plan.

69
00:06:36,591 --> 00:06:38,831
If it weren't for him, we would have been trapped.

70
00:06:39,471 --> 00:06:39,791
Yeah.

71
00:06:53,071 --> 00:06:56,751
We can still attack from the front and the rear, even if they're not closed in the bay.

72
00:06:57,311 --> 00:07:00,271
Stick to the plan and take down the Allied forces first!

73
00:07:01,231 --> 00:07:04,911
Eliminate any pirate that's trying to stray from the enclosure to advance!

74
00:07:08,031 --> 00:07:09,071
And there you go!

75
00:07:10,271 --> 00:07:10,831
Got it!

76
00:07:10,831 --> 00:07:13,071
And if our ships get caught in the crossfire?

77
00:07:13,071 --> 00:07:15,231
Let's try to keep it to a minimum, okay?

78
00:07:15,231 --> 00:07:17,391
So that's the plan, huh?

79
00:07:18,911 --> 00:07:21,071
Then, time to work!

80
00:07:21,071 --> 00:07:21,871
Quick!

81
00:07:33,151 --> 00:07:34,911
Light up as many kumas as you want!

82
00:07:35,631 --> 00:07:36,991
We'll knock them down!

83
00:07:36,991 --> 00:07:38,111
We'll knock them down!

84
00:07:54,111 --> 00:07:54,911
No!

85
00:07:54,911 --> 00:07:55,471
No!

86
00:07:55,471 --> 00:07:55,951
Please!

87
00:08:06,991 --> 00:08:08,191
We'll knock them down!

88
00:08:12,271 --> 00:08:13,471
Now fire!

89
00:08:13,471 --> 00:08:14,671
Lots of pieces!

90
00:08:31,311 --> 00:08:32,431
They vaporized them!

91
00:08:36,991 --> 00:09:00,671
They're even willing to sacrifice their own men!

92
00:09:00,671 --> 00:09:09,711
Don't lose faith!

93
00:09:09,711 --> 00:09:10,991
March on!

94
00:09:11,951 --> 00:09:14,751
Charge the plaza with all of your might!

95
00:09:30,671 --> 00:09:34,111
The only retreat I know is death!

96
00:09:35,631 --> 00:09:38,751
But I'll rescue Ace before they can send me down that road!

97
00:09:45,471 --> 00:09:47,391
Everyone! Get off the ship now!

98
00:09:48,111 --> 00:09:50,351
Destroy those mechanical monsters!

99
00:09:50,351 --> 00:09:50,991
Yeah!

100
00:09:58,511 --> 00:09:59,311
Have at you!

101
00:10:01,951 --> 00:10:03,711
I shall not falter!

102
00:10:15,551 --> 00:10:18,831
All units, get off the ice and defend the front line now!

103
00:10:18,831 --> 00:10:23,791
Do whatever it takes to ensure the pirates don't reach the plaza!

104
00:10:23,791 --> 00:10:25,551
Go! Fall back!

105
00:10:28,031 --> 00:10:28,431
Hurry!

106
00:10:42,431 --> 00:10:47,471
It's quite the unexpected pleasure to cross blades with the world's greatest swordsman!

107
00:10:49,471 --> 00:10:51,151
Aren't I a lucky guy?

108
00:10:52,671 --> 00:10:55,391
Your swordsmanship is of no small renown either!

109
00:10:56,031 --> 00:10:57,631
We were certain to cross paths!

110
00:10:58,271 --> 00:10:59,551
Now show me your skill!

111
00:11:00,671 --> 00:11:02,431
I'm happy to give you a peek!

112
00:11:03,551 --> 00:11:04,831
Rose Rondo!

113
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:18,031
Father Rondo!

114
00:11:18,351 --> 00:11:30,191
What flowers would you like on your ground?

115
00:11:30,191 --> 00:11:35,191
What flowers would you like on your grave?

116
00:11:43,191 --> 00:11:46,191
Onward! Drive them in!

117
00:11:46,191 --> 00:11:47,191
Hell no!

118
00:11:51,191 --> 00:11:53,191
How's that feel?

119
00:12:00,191 --> 00:12:08,191
There's no way those things are made of flesh and bone.

120
00:12:08,191 --> 00:12:10,191
Well, they're obviously not human.

121
00:12:10,191 --> 00:12:12,191
Then what are they?

122
00:12:16,191 --> 00:12:18,191
Hey, what happened to the screen?

123
00:12:18,191 --> 00:12:31,191
Struggle all you want, Whitebeard.

124
00:12:31,191 --> 00:12:36,191
We still have the upper hand, ready to crush you.

125
00:12:36,191 --> 00:12:41,191
As soon as every video feed has been cut, activate the encircling walls.

126
00:12:41,191 --> 00:12:48,191
And once that's set, we will immediately execute Ace and round up all of our remaining enemies.

127
00:12:48,191 --> 00:12:50,191
Yes, sir!

128
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:57,191
Move it!

129
00:13:05,191 --> 00:13:08,191
They're about to kill Ace! I'd better hurry!

130
00:13:11,191 --> 00:13:13,191
Sorry, back to square one!

131
00:13:15,191 --> 00:13:16,191
Luffy, no!

132
00:13:26,191 --> 00:13:27,191
Team Bay!

133
00:13:32,191 --> 00:13:34,191
The Admiral's getting in on the fight!

134
00:13:35,191 --> 00:13:36,191
Damn it!

135
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,191
Yet we must press on regardless.

136
00:13:39,191 --> 00:13:43,191
We knew we would face insurmountable odds and undefeatable foes.

137
00:13:43,191 --> 00:13:46,191
Them sending out their best only means we're too close for their comfort.

138
00:13:50,191 --> 00:13:52,191
Time to die, son of dragon.

139
00:14:00,191 --> 00:14:01,191
Hey, Ace's brother.

140
00:14:01,191 --> 00:14:03,191
You're not running out of steam, are ya?

141
00:14:03,191 --> 00:14:04,191
Huh?

142
00:14:09,191 --> 00:14:10,191
Whitebeard's commanders!

143
00:14:10,191 --> 00:14:13,191
We won't find any better backup than that!

144
00:14:14,191 --> 00:14:16,191
You can't let one man halt your advance!

145
00:14:16,191 --> 00:14:17,191
Now follow us!

146
00:14:18,191 --> 00:14:19,191
Yeah!

147
00:14:19,191 --> 00:14:20,191
Let's take him!

148
00:14:20,191 --> 00:14:22,191
The Navy's pulling back, so now's our chance!

149
00:14:23,191 --> 00:14:25,191
We're breaking through these bastards!

150
00:14:26,191 --> 00:14:27,191
Ooh!

151
00:14:27,191 --> 00:14:28,191
Looky here!

152
00:14:28,191 --> 00:14:29,191
It's a real fight!

153
00:14:33,191 --> 00:14:58,051
This game is done to deliver the

154
00:14:58,051 --> 00:14:59,811
Commander Kuriel.

155
00:14:59,811 --> 00:15:01,471
Look at that angry glower.

156
00:15:01,471 --> 00:15:05,611
Do you really want to die with such a sour face?

157
00:15:05,611 --> 00:15:09,471
You do realize you'll be buried in this bay if you stay here.

158
00:15:09,471 --> 00:15:11,471
First, Ace will die.

159
00:15:11,471 --> 00:15:14,571
And then your cronies will be trapped and wiped out.

160
00:15:14,571 --> 00:15:16,611
I honestly couldn't care less about who's

161
00:15:16,611 --> 00:15:20,171
going to win this war but watching Whitebeard die?

162
00:15:20,171 --> 00:15:22,531
That's fun!

163
00:15:22,531 --> 00:15:24,011
Pops and Ace won't die.

164
00:15:24,011 --> 00:15:25,171
Not while I'm around!

165
00:15:28,051 --> 00:15:37,091
Shall we put this match on hold?

166
00:15:37,091 --> 00:15:38,091
Vista.

167
00:15:38,091 --> 00:15:42,931
Much as I hate to, we do have other matters to worry about.

168
00:15:42,931 --> 00:15:48,931
We've got to back down, so let's go, Smoker.

169
00:15:48,931 --> 00:15:53,931
Didn't you hear the orders?

170
00:15:53,931 --> 00:16:01,311
Yeah, I heard him.

171
00:16:01,311 --> 00:16:02,971
Next time, Straw Hat.

172
00:16:02,971 --> 00:16:12,011
Luffy, you can do it.

173
00:16:12,011 --> 00:16:13,011
Stay strong.

174
00:16:13,011 --> 00:16:15,351
Where the hell has the video feed been cut?

175
00:16:15,351 --> 00:16:16,351
Sorry, sir.

176
00:16:16,351 --> 00:16:17,351
It'll just be another minute.

177
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:18,011
Hey, have you found it?

178
00:16:18,011 --> 00:16:19,011
Uh, no.

179
00:16:19,011 --> 00:16:21,011
We're still searching, but it's just gone missing.

180
00:16:21,011 --> 00:16:33,391
We're all set.

181
00:16:33,391 --> 00:16:36,051
Hey, Gaffer, you're blocking the shot.

182
00:16:36,051 --> 00:16:39,771
It seems like they've cut all the camera feeds except for one.

183
00:16:39,771 --> 00:16:41,391
But what's with this stupid message?

184
00:16:41,391 --> 00:16:52,311
Just show us already.

185
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:53,431
The camera's good to go.

186
00:16:53,431 --> 00:16:54,431
Okay, then.

187
00:16:54,431 --> 00:17:01,351
We're going live in five, four, three, two, one, action!

188
00:17:01,351 --> 00:17:04,731
Hey, it came back on.

189
00:17:04,731 --> 00:17:08,731
So, um, uh, sorry.

190
00:17:08,731 --> 00:17:10,731
We apologize for keeping you waiting.

191
00:17:10,731 --> 00:17:12,731
Wait, who is that talking?

192
00:17:12,731 --> 00:17:19,731
Uh, we're live here at Marineford, surrounded by the dead bodies of pirates and marines.

193
00:17:19,731 --> 00:17:21,731
They're doing a commentary?

194
00:17:21,731 --> 00:17:25,731
Hey, what's going on down there?

195
00:17:25,731 --> 00:17:26,731
What is this feed?

196
00:17:26,731 --> 00:17:29,731
Wait, is that who I think it is?

197
00:17:29,731 --> 00:17:31,731
Oh, it is!

198
00:17:31,731 --> 00:17:33,731
I can't believe it's him!

199
00:17:33,731 --> 00:17:36,731
He's been laying low for all these years, but...

200
00:17:36,731 --> 00:17:42,731
He was a member of the legendary crew that served under Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates!

201
00:17:42,731 --> 00:17:43,731
Huh?

202
00:17:43,731 --> 00:17:44,731
Who is it?

203
00:17:44,731 --> 00:17:48,731
Can it really be the renowned pirate, Captain Buggy?

204
00:17:48,731 --> 00:17:49,731
Huh?

205
00:17:49,731 --> 00:17:53,731
I'm sorry, did someone say my name?

206
00:17:53,731 --> 00:17:54,731
Huh?

207
00:17:54,731 --> 00:17:56,731
Huh?

208
00:17:56,731 --> 00:18:00,731
It is classified information, but I admit it.

209
00:18:00,731 --> 00:18:03,731
I am the legendary pirate!

210
00:18:03,731 --> 00:18:04,731
Hey!

211
00:18:04,731 --> 00:18:05,731
Hold it, Captain Buggy!

212
00:18:05,731 --> 00:18:06,731
Stop!

213
00:18:06,731 --> 00:18:08,731
You've got a nose blade!

214
00:18:08,731 --> 00:18:18,731
What the hell is happening here?

215
00:18:18,731 --> 00:18:23,731
How many times have I ordered you fools to catch this stupid video?

216
00:18:23,731 --> 00:18:25,731
We can't move without world watching!

217
00:18:25,731 --> 00:18:32,731
I understand, sir, but I'm afraid that the escaped prisoners have somehow managed to steal one of the video transponder snails from us!

218
00:18:32,731 --> 00:18:33,731
What?!

219
00:18:33,731 --> 00:18:36,731
How did you let this happen?!

220
00:18:36,731 --> 00:18:37,731
Make up!

221
00:18:37,731 --> 00:18:38,731
Ready to roll!

222
00:18:38,731 --> 00:18:40,731
Alright guys, mark it!

223
00:18:40,731 --> 00:18:45,731
Take two, in three, two, one, and...

224
00:18:45,731 --> 00:18:46,731
Oh!

225
00:18:46,731 --> 00:18:48,731
Is that who I think it is?

226
00:18:48,731 --> 00:18:54,731
The legendary crew member of Gold Roger and the sworn brother of Shanks of the Four Emperors?

227
00:18:54,731 --> 00:18:58,731
Could it really be the mythical pirate, Captain Buggy?

228
00:18:58,731 --> 00:19:00,731
Did someone say my name?!

229
00:19:00,731 --> 00:19:04,731
Stop those idiots right this second!

230
00:19:04,731 --> 00:19:07,731
Whoa, that was close!

231
00:19:07,731 --> 00:19:08,731
They bound us!

232
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:09,731
Run for it!

233
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:15,731
I just saw you get sliced in half by the infamous Hawkeye Mihawk!

234
00:19:15,731 --> 00:19:18,731
But there's not even a scratch on you!

235
00:19:18,731 --> 00:19:21,731
Who, me?

236
00:19:21,731 --> 00:19:22,731
That's right!

237
00:19:22,731 --> 00:19:23,731
I'm Buggy!

238
00:19:23,731 --> 00:19:25,731
The living legend!

239
00:19:25,731 --> 00:19:26,731
Blow them away!

240
00:19:26,731 --> 00:19:28,731
I want them dead!

241
00:19:28,731 --> 00:19:31,731
Cut back to the war, dammit!

242
00:19:31,731 --> 00:19:33,731
Why are we getting video of this, moron?!

243
00:19:33,731 --> 00:19:34,731
Go back to Ace!

244
00:19:34,731 --> 00:19:36,731
We're gonna miss the execution!

245
00:19:36,731 --> 00:19:41,731
I want to see that army apart while with you kumars!

246
00:19:49,731 --> 00:19:55,731
They're driving us into a corner!

247
00:19:55,731 --> 00:19:57,731
Stand tall, men!

248
00:19:57,731 --> 00:19:59,731
We can't stop now!

249
00:19:59,731 --> 00:20:01,731
Not until we know that Ace is safe!

250
00:20:01,731 --> 00:20:02,731
Let's go!

251
00:20:06,731 --> 00:20:07,731
Get ready!

252
00:20:07,731 --> 00:20:08,731
Fire!

253
00:20:08,731 --> 00:20:09,731
Fire!

254
00:20:09,731 --> 00:20:10,731
Fire!

255
00:20:10,731 --> 00:20:11,731
Fire!

256
00:20:23,731 --> 00:20:25,731
Hey, Pops!

257
00:20:25,731 --> 00:20:29,731
Hey, Pops.

258
00:20:33,731 --> 00:20:36,731
Oh, Squared. Good to see you're alive.

259
00:20:36,731 --> 00:20:38,731
Yeah, barely.

260
00:20:38,731 --> 00:20:41,731
Is that so? I was trying to reach you earlier.

261
00:20:41,731 --> 00:20:44,731
How are things looking at the Bayhead now?

262
00:20:44,731 --> 00:20:48,731
I'm sorry to say, but your allies were beaten pretty badly.

263
00:20:48,731 --> 00:20:52,731
As for me, I only managed to get out of there through sheer luck.

264
00:20:52,731 --> 00:20:58,731
Sengoku is one merciless bastard. He's pulling out every dirty trick he can think of.

265
00:20:58,731 --> 00:21:03,731
Judging by your shift in tactic, I'm guessing you picked up on the Navy's plan.

266
00:21:03,731 --> 00:21:07,731
I've known Sengoku and what he's capable of for a long time.

267
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:15,731
I see.

268
00:21:15,731 --> 00:21:19,731
Little does he know it works in our favor for them to attack us from the rear.

269
00:21:19,731 --> 00:21:24,731
I'm joining the fight. Our only chance is to keep pushing forward.

270
00:21:24,731 --> 00:21:26,731
I couldn't agree more.

271
00:21:28,731 --> 00:21:30,731
What's Squared doing up there?

272
00:21:30,731 --> 00:21:34,731
You have 43 allied captains willing to die for you.

273
00:21:34,731 --> 00:21:38,731
We're all in your debt, for now and for always.

274
00:21:38,731 --> 00:21:42,731
We consider it a privilege to risk our lives for you and your crew.

275
00:21:42,731 --> 00:21:50,731
And I'm grateful.

276
00:21:50,731 --> 00:21:52,731
But this fight is...

277
00:21:52,731 --> 00:21:53,731
Yes, I know.

278
00:21:53,731 --> 00:21:56,731
This fight is to save a member of your family.

279
00:21:56,731 --> 00:22:01,731
The great pirate Whitebeard is a man who would do anything for his family.

280
00:22:01,731 --> 00:22:04,731
And your loyalty inspires loyalty.

281
00:22:04,731 --> 00:22:07,731
That's why everyone followed you to this hell.

282
00:22:07,731 --> 00:22:13,731
I do wish things were different.

283
00:22:13,731 --> 00:22:17,731
But at the end of the day...

284
00:22:17,731 --> 00:22:21,731
I'm not a part of your family.

285
00:22:21,731 --> 00:22:24,731
It's not a part of your family.

286
00:22:24,731 --> 00:22:27,731
It's not a part of your family.

287
00:22:27,731 --> 00:22:31,731
Uh oh...

288
00:22:31,731 --> 00:22:34,731
Massa Walla

289
00:22:37,731 --> 00:22:41,731
Taliesa

290
00:22:41,731 --> 00:22:43,531
Oh, thank you.

291
00:23:11,731 --> 00:23:14,671
After witnessing Squard's betrayal against Whitebeard,

292
00:23:14,671 --> 00:23:18,211
ripples of distrust and uncertainty spread within his alliance.

293
00:23:18,211 --> 00:23:20,731
And yet Whitebeard's faith will not be shattered,

294
00:23:20,731 --> 00:23:23,311
and it soon becomes clear that his allies are falling

295
00:23:23,311 --> 00:23:26,111
into a clever setup launched by the Navy.

296
00:23:26,111 --> 00:23:31,691
On the next, One Piece, Akainu's plot, Whitebeard entrapped.

297
00:23:31,691 --> 00:23:34,491
I'm going to be king of the pirates.

